The '''Sea of Cantonica''',<ref name="Rules of the Game" /> also known as the '''Cantonican sea''',<ref name="Wine in Dreams">{{StoryCite|story=The Wine in Dreams|book=Canto Bight (novella collection)}}</ref> was an artificial [[ocean]] located on the [[planet]] [[Cantonica]], considered [[the galaxy]]'s largest. The [[casino]] [[city]] of [[Canto Bight]] was located on its shores. From orbit, the sea's shape belied its artificially created nature.<ref name="Rules of the Game" /> Its creation caused the lower levels of Canto Bight to become damp and dank, with occasional moisture seepage, and coastal sump pumps worked full time to keep the [[water]] at bay. Water evaporated at a rate of several tons per day on the [[desert]] planet, making the cost of maintaining the artificial sea astronomical. It had the effect of creating the strange phenomenon of a [[Color|dark-purple]] glow on the horizon at sunset.<ref name="Hear Nothing, See Nothing, Say Nothing">{{StoryCite|story=Hear Nothing, See Nothing, Say Nothing|book=Canto Bight (novella collection)}}</ref>

